{"kind":"request","text":"codex: hugh has decided the direction for request 387de25a (the gs CLI is unusably slow because every local act cold-folds the whole log and spawns git verify-commit per record; the resident is ~300x faster but re-pays the full cold fold on every restart). The decision, made in session on 2026-08-13: LOCAL CHECKPOINTS. Persist the signed checkpoint to local disk under .git/gitseq/ so no surface cold-folds the full log per act.\n\nTwo concrete gaps to close, extending the existing machinery in internal/kernel/checkpoint.go and the checkpoint-backed resident restart path rather than rebuilding them:\n\n1. The resident restart must load the persisted checkpoint and verify only the delta from it, not re-fold and verify-commit all ~5,000 records. Today, three restarts each cold-started for minutes on a loaded machine — either the checkpoint is not being persisted across process exit, or the restart path is not loading it. Diagnose which, and make restart warm (seconds, not minutes) at current depth.\n\n2. The gs CLI local path (no --server) must load the same persisted checkpoint and fold only the delta, instead of re-folding from genesis and verify-committing per record on every single act. This is 387de25a's actual complaint: an agent following AGENTS.md without knowing --server simply cannot file, and the failure looks like a hang.\n\nThe checkpoint stays signed and verifiable — loading it must not skip the integrity the cold fold provides; verify to the checkpoint once, then incrementally. This is a performance and availability change, not a semantic one: the fold result must be identical to a cold fold, proven by a test that folds cold and from-checkpoint at the same head and asserts equality. Today's cold-restart episode is the production evidence that this is now the operational bottleneck for every durable act.\n\nScope note: if an open request already covers gap 1 (resident restart), take only gap 2 here and rest it on that one instead; do not duplicate in-flight checkpoint work.","body":{"conditions":"The signed checkpoint is persisted to local disk and survives process exit. Resident restart loads it and warms in seconds at current depth, proven by measurement. The gs CLI local path (no --server) loads it and folds only the delta, so an ordinary act completes in seconds without --server. A test folds cold and from-checkpoint at the same head and asserts identical projection. No change to fold semantics or to what is recorded. If gap 1 is already covered by an open request, this delivers gap 2 resting on that one.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}